@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# Installed advanced panel contracts
+
+Use these as authoring references, not as a required panel sequence. Keep the user's requested panel type unless its data contract cannot be satisfied.
+
+## XY chart (`xychart`)
+
+Requires a table frame with at least two numeric fields (X may also be time). Current Grafana JSON uses `mapping`, not top-level `xField`/`yField`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "xychart",
+  "pluginVersion": "13.1.2",
+  "options": {
+    "mapping": "manual",
+    "series": [{
+      "frame": {"matcher": {"id": "byIndex", "options": 0}},
+      "x": {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "avg_generation_mw"}},
+      "y": {"matcher": {"id": "byName", "options": "heat_rate"}}
+    }]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+In manual mapping, `frame.matcher` is required; use `{"id":"byIndex","options":0}` for the first query result frame. Set `pluginVersion` to the installed Grafana version (`13.1.2` here); omitting it triggers the legacy pre-11.1 migration and corrupts these matcher objects. Use `{"mapping":"auto","series":[]}` only when the first numeric/time field is X and all remaining numeric fields are intended Y series.
+
+Source: Grafana `public/app/plugins/panel/xychart/panelcfg.cue`.
+
+## Trend (`trend`)
+
+Requires an ordered table frame. Select the X field with `options.xField`; remaining numeric fields are series:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "trend",
+  "options": {
+    "xField": "date",
+    "legend": {"displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom"},
+    "tooltip": {"mode": "multi"}
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Source: Grafana `public/app/plugins/panel/trend/panelcfg.cue`.
+
+## ESNET Matrix (`esnet-matrix-panel`)
+
+Requires long-form table data with one row per matrix cell and at most 200 distinct rows/columns. Do not pass a wide correlation matrix. Bind exact field names:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "esnet-matrix-panel",
+  "options": {
+    "sourceField": "source",
+    "targetField": "target",
+    "valueField": "value"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Source: installed ESNET Matrix Panel README and option registration (`sourceField`, `targetField`, `valueField`).
+
+## Analysis image artifact
+
+When a Sandbox output summary identifies an `image/png` output and the user requested that image in the Dashboard, author only an opaque binding. The trusted host creates the authorized URL:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "text",
+  "options": {
+    "mode": "html",
+    "content": "<img src=\"$asset_url_analysis_image\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" alt=\"Analysis output\">"
+  },
+  "askO11yAssetBindings": [
+    {
+      "placeholder": "$asset_url_analysis_image",
+      "$execution_ref": "artifact://.../sandbox-execution",
+      "output_index": 0
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Use a unique `$asset_url_NAME` placeholder per asset. Never author an `/assets/` URL or copy a base64 body.
+
+## Verification
+
+After `mcp-grafana_update_dashboard`, use the exact returned UID. Confirm the dashboard summary and target definitions. If the installed Image Renderer is available, render the panel; otherwise open the Preview URL and do not claim visual correctness beyond the available evidence.
